PWM: Pulse Width Modulation in Embedded C
PWM is a technique used to control the average power delivered to a device by switching a digital
signal ON and OFF very quickly.

It is widely used in industrial embedded system for motor speed control, LED brightness, heater control, and
power electronics.

1. How PWM works
Imagine controlling a motor using a switch. Instead of keeping the switch ON continuously, you turn it ON and
OFF rapidly.
- ON Time: power is delivered
- OFF TIme: power is not delivered
- Duty Cycle: percentage of each period that the signal stays ON

